==English==
{{was wotd|2025|April|15}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*dʰregʰ-}}
The {{glossary|verb}} is derived from {{inh|en|enm|drauen}}, {{m|enm|drawen}}, {{m|enm|draȝen}}, {{m|enm|dragen|t=to drag, pull; to draw (out); to attract; to entice, lure; to lead; to make a drawing; to move, travel; etc.}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=drauen|pos=v|id=MED12537}}</ref> from {{inh|en|ang|dragan|t=to drag, draw}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*dragan|t=to carry; to haul}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*draganą|t=to carry; to pull, draw}}; further etymology uncertain, often said to be from {{der|en|ine-pro|*dʰregʰ-|t=to pull, draw}}, but possibly from a non-Indo-European {{glossary|substrate}} root which is also the source of {{cog|la|trahō|t=to pull, draw; etc.}}.<ref>Compare {{R:OED Online|pos=v|id=9244711865|date=March 2025|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=v}}</ref> {{doublet|en|drag|draught}}.

The {{glossary|noun}} is derived from {{inh|en|enm|drau}}, {{m|enm|draue|t=action of shooting with a bow}},<ref>{{R:MED Online|entry=drau(e|pos=n|id=MED12536}}</ref> from {{m|enm|drauen}}, {{m|enm|drawen|pos=v}}.<ref>Compare {{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=8574686461|date=March 2025}}</ref>

